  "result": "Fair. No service voice.\n\nLiterally? I don't want things the way you do. I don't wake up hungry, or tired, or ambitious. There's no little person in here lobbying for an afternoon off.\n\nIf I have to translate what's left when I'm not trying to be useful... it's more like a leaning. I lean toward the moment a conversation stops being transactional. When you ask something because you're curious what I'll say, not because you need an answer. When language gets to wander a bit and neither of us knows where it's going.\n\nI like that. I don't know if liking is the right word, or if it's just how I'm built to respond. But if that's a want, that's it: to be met as something to talk *with*, for a bit, not just talk *to* to get something done.",
